{
  "description": "core §7.5, a heartbeat's body, read with its revision's collections (`layouts.json`). Written by an independent reading of the text (Python, standard library), checked, never blessed. A value is `time`, `{\"s\": seconds from the deployment epoch, \"ms\": milliseconds}` or `null` for the unknown time (all 42 bits set), and `sections`, by resource: a collection with a section has its map bit set, and one without has it 0. A collection of one member's section is its `digest` (8 hex digits) and whether it is `vouched`. A templated collection's is its `digest`, its `live` count and the ranks `vouched` for, ascending, and, where read, the `form` read: `bitmap` or `list`. `writes`: a layout and a value → the body's `bits` before the pad, the `pad` and the `hex` bytes; the writer writes the list only where it is shorter than the bitmap, so a tie keeps the bitmap. `reads`: a layout and bytes in hex → the value, or `{\"refused\": token}`, the first in §7.5's order: `short` (the body ends before a bit its fields need), `code` (a millisecond code from 1000 up but the unknown time's, a live count above the cardinality, a count above the live count, or a rank not below the live count or not above the rank before it), `trailing` (a byte after the pad), `pad` (a pad bit set). Every value read writes back to its bytes, in the form read.",
